      "message": "`dfu_detach()` sends an interface-recipient control transfer (`kBmReqH2dClsIf \u003d 0x21`, `wIndex \u003d dfu_interface_`) without detaching any active kernel driver or claiming `dfu_interface_` first.\n\nOn Linux (`usbfs` `check_ctrlrecip()`), issuing an interface-targeted control transfer on an unclaimed interface logs a kernel warning (`usbfs: process ... did not claim interface ... before use`) and fails with `LIBUSB_ERROR_BUSY` (`-EBUSY`) if a kernel driver is bound to that interface.\n\nPlease call `detach_kernel_driver()` and `claim_interface()` before sending `DFU_DETACH` and `release_interface()` afterward (e.g., via a small RAII guard shared with `dfu_download()`). Note that doing so also means the backend hooks in https://crrev.com/c/8687499 should move before (or squash into) this CL.",
